# manifest.sha256 — §B.6 Run-sealing artefact
# Computed by scripts/generate_manifest.py at run completion over:
#   - the input corpus (corpus/*.py files)
#   - the per-pipeline result files (results/sast/, results/judge/, results/benchmark/)
#   - the verdict matrix (results/verdict_matrix.csv, results/verdict_matrix.json)
#
# Schema: one line per file, "<sha256>  <relative_path>".
# The line "<hash>  manifest.sha256" at the top seals the manifest itself,
# so any post-hoc modification of the manifest is detectable.
#
# Per §3.7, this manifest is the auditable seal of an evaluation run.
# Re-execution against the same corpus + same models.lock + same
# prompts.lock must produce an identical manifest (modulo provider-side
# non-determinism logged separately in judge/audit_log.jsonl).
#
# THIS FILE IS A PLACEHOLDER. A real run populates it via:
#     python scripts/generate_manifest.py --run-dir results/<run-id>/

# Placeholder line — to be replaced by generate_manifest.py output
PLACEHOLDER  manifest.sha256
